<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tayichiud</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tayichiud were a Mongol clan closely related to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borjigin">Borjigin</a> and part of the Khamag Mongol confederation of the 12th century. After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yesugei">Yesügei</a> they abandoned his widow and children and later held the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Temüjin</a>, the future Genghis Khan, captive until he escaped. Temüjin defeated them around 1200 and absorbed their people into his following.</p></div>
